+3. Revise scenario JSON using fields listed in attached instructions.
+4. List commands that complete your game and one command that should fail, then open your game.
+5. Compare a submitted record with expected behavior.</pre></div></div></section><section aria-label="Slide 16: Specify Format" aria-roledescription="slide" class="slide layout-content" data-group="Draft" data-original="skills:23" data-title="Specify Format" role="group" tabindex="-1"><div class="slide-inner"><h2>Specify Format</h2><p>Separate your game file, source evidence, and test results.</p><div class="prompt-container"><button class="copy-btn" data-copy="skills-tpl-format">Copy prompt</button><pre class="prompt-block" id="skills-tpl-format">Scenario JSON: [Complete scenario]
 Source: [Relevant historical passage]
 Invented elements: [Rooms or simplified observations]
